<http://data.silknow.org/object/e85edb8b-4c0f-3546-b057-d5f6377ffd5b/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/general-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Cream white cotton with designs commemorating fall of Bastille and Louis XVI, printed in dark neutral violet. Background covered with flowers, ribbons, fleur-de-lis, and medallions with scenes, or inscriptions in French and Latin. Under fall of Bastille is \"Gordon Sculp\" in very small letters. On barrel-head near monument to Louis XVI are letters \"WS\" and \"SR\". Lined with cotton printed with small all-over design in neutral tones and quilted with thin filling of cotton wool."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/e85edb8b-4c0f-3546-b057-d5f6377ffd5b> .

